            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Pasteur Institute</strong><br>\nTo continue his research and provide a space for scientific studies in microbiology, Pasteur founded the Pasteur Institute in 1887. The institute became a leading center for medical research and education, contributing to the study and treatment of infectious diseases.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Legacy in Science and Medicine</strong><br>\nLouis Pasteur's contributions to science and medicine are immeasurable. His dedication to understanding disease has saved countless lives. His work laid the groundwork for hygiene, public health, and much of modern medicine. He died on September 28, 1895, leaving behind a legacy that continues to benefit humanity.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Honors and Memory</strong><br>\nPasteur's impact was recognized globally during his lifetime and after. He received numerous awards and honors, including the Legion of Honor from France. Schools, institutions, and awards have been named in his honor, ensuring that his contributions to science and public health are remembered.</p>\n"
              },
